//
//  Lineage : split out of the "IBSFade" multi-strategy indicator, DataBox plot #24.
//  Provenance: Practitioner pattern rules; only Turtle Soup has a published rule set (Connors & Raschke,
//            Street Smarts 1995) and this implementation omits its prior-extreme age condition.
//            Confidence values are heuristic constants.
//  Concept : Liquidity sweeps (stop hunts) of swing / key levels, Swing Failure
//            Pattern, equal-high/low traps, consolidation breakout traps, Wyckoff
//            Spring / Upthrust, Turtle Soup (Connors & Raschke 1995) and
//            volume-divergence fakeouts with a 3-bar confirmation window.
//  Output  : price-panel labels "Liq Sweep Start: <patterns> (conf%)" and
//            "Liq Sweep End: <patterns> (conf%)", a dashed Start->End connecting
//            line, and two panel plots: Confidence (0..1, 0 when nothing fired)
//            and Structure (+1 bullish, -1 bearish, 0 none).
//  Quirks preserved from ORIG:
//            - Detection starts at CurrentBar >= SwingLookback*2+5 (ORIG 2040),
//              on top of the global CurrentBar < 50 guard (ORIG 601).
//            - "Liq Sweep Start" labels (VolDiv, conf 0.35) are drawn inside the
//              pattern check itself and are NOT subject to DuplicateBarWindow
//              (ORIG 2308/2315). A confirmed pending sweep draws an End label with
//              conf 0.55 BEFORE the 7 checks run on that bar (ORIG 2171), which can
//              then suppress a same-direction End from the checks via the window.
//            - Swing points are confirmed SwingLookback bars late (pivot at High[lb]).
//            - Equal-level pool: max 10 entries, entries expire after 200 bars.
//            - Consolidation zone: ATR14/SMA50(ATR14) < ratio to enter; exits only
//              when ratio >= 1.5x AND more than 50 bars since start (ORIG 2150).
//            - Key-level checks use ORIG's RTH 8:30-16:00 CST / ORB 8:30-9:00 CST /
//              calendar-month tracking (ORIG 656-808, line drawing removed);
//              weekends keep Friday's values. Asian-session levels are not used by
//              any sweep check and are omitted.
//            - The volDelta series is maintained per ORIG 1623-1634 for parity with
//              the sibling modules, but no sweep check reads it.
// ============================================================================
